In addition, if we were treated as a PRC resident enterprise, any dividends payable to non-resident enterprise holders of our
common shares or ADSs may be treated as income derived from sources within PRC and therefore subject to a 10% withholding tax
(or 20% in the case of non-resident individual holders) unless an applicable income tax treaty provides otherwise. In addition, capital
gains realized by non-resident enterprise holders upon the disposition of our common shares or ADSs may be treated as income
derived from sources within PRC and therefore subject to 10% income tax (or 20% in the case of non-resident individual holders)
unless an applicable income tax treaty provides otherwise.
